{"id":"mahabharata-1-021","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":21,"title":"एकविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 21 · Kadru praises Indra","summary":{"en":"Garuda flies to his mother across the ocean and, at Kadru's bidding, carries the snakes on his back towards the sun, which scorches them. Kadru sings a hymn to Indra, lord of the clouds, begging him to save her sons.","kn":"ಗರುಡನು ಸಮುದ್ರದಾಚೆಯ ತಾಯಿಯ ಬಳಿಗೆ ಬಂದು ಕದ್ರುವಿನ ಆಜ್ಞೆಯಂತೆ ಹಾವುಗಳನ್ನು ಬೆನ್ನಮೇಲೆ ಹೊತ್ತು ಸೂರ್ಯನತ್ತ ಹಾರುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಬಿಸಿಲಿಗೆ ಅವು ಬೆಂದುಹೋಗುತ್ತವೆ. ಮಕ್ಕಳನ್ನು ಕಾಪಾಡೆಂದು ಕದ್ರು ಮೇಘಪತಿ ಇಂದ್ರನನ್ನು ಸ್ತುತಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"गरुड़ समुद्र पार माता के पास आते हैं और कद्रू की आज्ञा से साँपों को पीठ पर लादकर सूर्य की ओर उड़ते हैं, जिससे वे झुलस जाते हैं। कद्रू पुत्रों की रक्षा के लिए मेघों के स्वामी इन्द्र की स्तुति करती हैं।","te":"గరుడుడు సముద్రం దాటి తల్లి వద్దకు వచ్చి కద్రువ ఆజ్ఞ ప్రకారం పాములను వీపుపై మోస్తూ సూర్యుని వైపు ఎగురుతాడు, ఎండకు అవి మాడిపోతాయి. తన కుమారులను కాపాడమని కద్రువ మేఘపతి ఇంద్రుని స్తుతిస్తుంది.","ta":"கருடன் கடல் கடந்து தாயிடம் வந்து, கத்ருவின் ஆணைப்படி பாம்புகளை முதுகில் சுமந்து சூரியனை நோக்கிப் பறக்க, வெயிலில் அவை கருகுகின்றன. தன் மைந்தர்களைக் காக்குமாறு கத்ரு மேகங்களின் தலைவனான இந்திரனைத் துதிக்கிறாள்.","ml":"ഗരുഡൻ സമുദ്രം കടന്ന് അമ്മയുടെ അടുത്തെത്തുന്നു; കദ്രുവിന്റെ കല്പനപ്രകാരം പാമ്പുകളെ പുറത്തേറ്റി സൂര്യനിലേക്ക് കൊണ്ടുപോകുന്നു, സൂര്യൻ അവയെ പൊള്ളിക്കുന്നു. മേഘങ്ങളുടെ നാഥനായ ഇന്ദ്രനെ, തന്റെ പുത്രന്മാരെ രക്ഷിക്കണമെന്ന് യാചിച്ച് കദ്രു സ്തുതിഗീതം ചൊല്ലുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.21; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"आस्तीकपर्व","titleEn":"Astika Parva","verses":[{"text":"सूत उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Suta's son said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततः कामगमः पक्षी महावीर्यो महाबलः ।\nमातुरन्तिकमागच्छत्परं तीरं महोदधेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mighty and powerful bird, who goes where he wishes, came to his mother on the far shore of the great ocean."}},{"n":2,"text":"यत्र सा विनता तस्मिन्पणितेन पराजिता ।\nअतीव दुःखसंतप्ता दासीभावमुपागता ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Vinata, defeated in the wager, was suffering terribly and living as a slave."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततः कदाचिद्विनतां प्रवणां पुत्रसंनिधौ ।\nकाल आहूय वचनं कद्रूरिदमभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then one day, at the proper time, Kadru called Vinata, who was bowed before her son, and said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"नागानामालयं भद्रे सुरम्यं रमणीयकम् ।\nसमुद्रकुक्षावेकान्ते तत्र मां विनते वह ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Good lady, in a secluded place in the ocean's depths there is a lovely, delightful home of the nagas. Carry me there, Vinata.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"ततः सुपर्णमाता तामवहत्सर्पमातरम् ।\nपन्नगान्गरुडश्चापि मातुर्वचनचोदितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So Vinata, mother of Suparna, carried Kadru, mother of serpents, and Garuda too, prompted by his mother's word, carried the serpents."}},{"n":6,"text":"स सूर्यस्याभितो याति वैनतेयो विहंगमः ।\nसूर्यरश्मिपरीताश्च मूर्च्छिताः पन्नगाभवन् ।\nतदवस्थान्सुतान्दृष्ट्वा कद्रूः शक्रमथास्तुवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The bird son of Vinata flew toward the sun. The serpents, scorched by the sun's rays, fainted. Seeing her sons in this state, Kadru praised Indra."}},{"n":7,"text":"नमस्ते देवदेवेश नमस्ते बलसूदन ।\nनमुचिघ्न नमस्तेऽस्तु सहस्राक्ष शचीपते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Homage to you, god of gods. Homage to you, destroyer of Bala. Homage, slayer of Namuci, thousand-eyed husband of Shachi."}},{"n":8,"text":"सर्पाणां सूर्यतप्तानां वारिणा त्वं प्लवो भव ।\nत्वमेव परमं त्राणमस्माकममरोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Be a raft of water for the serpents scorched by the sun. You alone are our highest protection, best of the immortals."}},{"n":9,"text":"ईशो ह्यसि पयः स्रष्टुं त्वमनल्पं पुरंदर ।\nत्वमेव मेघस्त्वं वायुस्त्वमग्निर्वैद्युतोऽम्बरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"You, Purandara, are able to pour out abundant water. You are the cloud, the wind, and the lightning-fire in the sky."}},{"n":10,"text":"त्वमभ्रघनविक्षेप्ता त्वामेवाहुः पुनर्घनम् ।\nत्वं वज्रमतुलं घोरं घोषवांस्त्वं बलाहकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You scatter the dense clouds, and they call you the thickening cloud again. You are the incomparable, terrible thunderbolt, and the thundering rain cloud."}},{"n":11,"text":"स्रष्टा त्वमेव लोकानां संहर्ता चापराजितः ।\nत्वं ज्योतिः सर्वभूतानां त्वमादित्यो विभावसुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You alone are the creator of the worlds and their unconquered destroyer. You are the light of all beings, you are the sun and the fire."}},{"n":12,"text":"त्वं महद्भूतमाश्चर्यं त्वं राजा त्वं सुरोत्तमः ।\nत्वं विष्णुस्त्वं सहस्राक्षस्त्वं देवस्त्वं परायणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are the great, wondrous being; you are king, the best of the gods. You are Vishnu, the thousand-eyed, the god, the final refuge."}},{"n":13,"text":"त्वं सर्वममृतं देव त्वं सोमः परमार्चितः ।\nत्वं मुहूर्तस्तिथिश्च त्वं लवस्त्वं वै पुनः क्षणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are all, the nectar, god; you are Soma, supremely honored. You are the muhurta and the lunar day, the lava, and again the kshana."}},{"n":14,"text":"शुक्लस्त्वं बहुलश्चैव कला काष्ठा त्रुटिस्तथा ।\nसंवत्सरर्तवो मासा रजन्यश्च दिनानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are the bright and the dark fortnight, the kala, the kashtha and the truti, the year, the seasons, the months, nights and days."}},{"n":15,"text":"त्वमुत्तमा सगिरिवना वसुंधरा\nसभास्करं वितिमिरमम्बरं तथा ।\nमहोदधिः सतिमितिमिंगिलस्तथा\nमहोर्मिमान्बहुमकरो झषालयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are the best earth with its mountains and forests, the sky with its sun and free of darkness, the great ocean with its huge fish and whales, with great waves, many crocodiles and a home for fish."}},{"n":16,"text":"महद्यशस्त्वमिति सदाभिपूज्यसे\nमनीषिभिर्मुदितमना महर्षिभिः ।\nअभिष्टुतः पिबसि च सोममध्वरे\nवषट्कृतान्यपि च हवींषि भूतये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great is your glory, so wise and great sages always worship you with joyful minds. Praised, you drink soma at the sacrifice, and the oblations offered with the vashat cry, for the sake of all beings."}},{"n":17,"text":"त्वं विप्रैः सततमिहेज्यसे फलार्थं\nवेदाङ्गेष्वतुलबलौघ गीयसे च ।\nत्वद्धेतोर्यजनपरायणा द्विजेन्द्रा\nवेदाङ्गान्यभिगमयन्ति सर्ववेदैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins constantly worship you here for rewards, and you are sung of in the Vedangas, you of limitless power. For your sake the best of the twice-born, devoted to sacrifice, study the Vedangas with all the Vedas.\""}}]}]}